  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 4971c5eb32d68c6419c2b82ec69e3fa3, type: 3}
  m_Name: ConvoStareThree
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::NarratorEventData
  eventID: ConvoStareThree
  dialogueLines:
  - The player is still listening. The narrator has noticed, and their patience is
    running out.
  - This has gone on long enough. The narrator is beginning to consider taking action.
  - The player continues to eavesdrop. Any longer, and the narrator may have to intervene.
  - The narrator has had enough of the snooping. The player should probably go away
    now.
  - The player really needs to stop listening. The narrator is very close to stepping
    in.
  - This is no longer just awkward. The narrator is running out of patience.
  - The player has pushed the snooping far enough. The narrator is prepared to intervene.
  - Still listening? The narrator is giving the player one final chance to go away.
  - The narrator has noticed exactly what the player is doing. They strongly suggest
    stopping now.
  - "That is quite enough snooping. If the player doesn\u2019t stop, the narrator
    will make them stop."
  canRepeat: 1
